# Initiatives

An initiative is an outcome several teams deliver over several quarters:
the program's Product Goal. The technical program manager writes and owns
it in this repository. Its requirement items are the outcomes a release
proves. Each sprint, every team gets a Sprint Goal issue that cites the
items it serves. An objective document under docs/specs/objectives/ is
read as an initiative.

## Documents here

- Name: `inNNN-short-name.md`, numbered in order and never reused.
- Format: an SRD in the pinned parent release's Markdown format, with the fields docs/constitutions/design.md lists for this level; tpm backlog template --kind initiative prints one in that layout.
- Status: `to_be_agreed` while it is drafted, `agreed` once it passes review, and `retired` when it is replaced. Only agreed documents are planned and rolled up. A retired document keeps its path, because links pin it.
- Parent: a theme. Epics name an initiative as theirs.
- Changes go through an issue and the corpus gate, never a direct edit on main.

## What reads them

- tpm goals plan and tpm goals push (the tasks skill) turn a release's initiative items into one Sprint Goal per team.
- tpm plan candidates and tpm plan write (the plan skill) place initiative items in a release on docs/road-map.md.

See tpm help backlog for the whole hierarchy.
